** Interpretive completion for the initial 2XMX interaction state.
**
** The surviving listing initializes DESIGNATED and CCENT to zero.  On the
** first CIRCLE CENTER command, DESIGNATE exchanges that zero CCENT into alpha.
** It then calls DELETE unless bit 1.1 of DESTS is one.  DELETE has no guard for
** object zero, so the printed zero default for automatic storage corrupts the
** DEADS ring.  The thesis says that the first CIRCLE CENTER command leaves a
** center point.  Therefore, the no-old-center sentinel must be one initially.
**
** The printed automatic-symbol table puts DESTS at 011444.  The current M4
** reconstruction puts it at 011411 because its RC/automatic interleaving is
** not yet historically exact.  This tape targets the current assembled
** address.  Update it when that remaining allocator difference is resolved.

 011411|
